<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hildebrand Veckinchusen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1370–<a href="/years/1426">1426</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hildebrand Veckinchusen was a Hanseatic merchant based mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a>, who with his brother Sivert traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a>, cloth, salt and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> and, briefly, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. Several hundred letters and account books of the family survive in the archives of Tallinn, one of the richest records of medieval Hanseatic commerce. Ruined by failed ventures and debt, he was imprisoned for debt in Bruges and died in 1426.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hildebrand-veckinchusen.jpg" alt="Hildebrand Veckinchusen" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hildebrand_Veckinchusen_-_Brief_18_Februar_1422_(letzte_Seite).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Merchant families such as the <b>Veckinchusens</b>, whose letters survive, operated through partnerships rather than large firms, and bookkeeping remained simple compared with Italy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=53.87,10.69&amp;year=1406" aria-label="Lübeck on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4787 314 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Hildebrand Veckinchusen"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5237 584h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5237 584h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=53.87,10.69&amp;year=1406">What was here in 1406? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
